## Trade-offs

| Decision | Benefit | Cost / Trade-off | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Supervisor + specialists (not monolith) | Localized testing, parallelism, clean audit attribution | More moving parts, orchestration code | Keep specialist set small (4); standardize evidence schema. |
| Deterministic scoring engine (not LLM scoring) | Reproducibility, auditability, tunable | Less "smart" nuance in scoring | LLM contributes *signals/anomalies as evidence*; scoring weights are config-driven and reviewable. |
| Parallel verification fan-out | Meets ≤30s SLA | Concurrency/error-handling complexity | Orchestrator enforces per-branch timeouts + partial-result handling. |
| LLM confined to extraction, anomaly reading, explanation | Limits hallucination blast radius | Requires strong grounding discipline | Narrative agent restricted to evidence bundle; extraction emits confidence for HITL. |
| External rule engine & vendor DB as tools | Reuses source-of-truth systems; no duplication | Dependency on external availability/latency | Timeouts, caching of FX/vendor reads, graceful degradation with explicit flags. |

---

## Rejected Alternatives

| Alternative | Why rejected |
|---|---|
| **Single monolithic agent** | Entangles OCR/extraction with verification; pushes deterministic checks into LLM (breaks reproducibility & audit); no parallelism (SLA risk); "never approve" becomes a prompt convention, not structural. |
| **Fully autonomous multi-agent swarm (e.g., market/blackboard with emergent coordination)** | Unnecessary nondeterminism and cost for a bounded, near-linear pipeline; harder to audit; coordination overhead with no decision-space benefit. |
| **Pure deterministic rules engine (no LLM at all)** | Cannot robustly handle OCR/extraction across heterogeneous formats or interpret nuanced format/tampering anomalies; brittle to layout variation. |
| **LLM-as-scorer (model outputs the reliability score directly)** | Violates reproducibility/auditability constraint; scores would drift and be hard to defend in audit/SOX context. |
| **Two-tier (extraction agent + one giant "validator" agent)** | Re-monolithizes verification; loses per-check attribution and independent tuning of vendor/duplicate/policy/integrity metrics. |

