## 2. Stage Map & Concurrency Model

```
STAGE A (sequential gate)          STAGE B (parallel fan-out)        STAGE C → D → E (sequential)
┌──────────────┐                   ┌──────────────────────────┐
│  A1 Extraction│  ──gate pass──▶  │  ┌─A2 Vendor──────────┐   │     ┌─T1 Score─┐  ┌─A6 Narrate─┐  ┌─Handoff─┐
│  (+T2 FX)     │                   │  ├─A3 Duplicate───────┤   │ ──▶ │ determ.  │─▶│   LLM      │─▶│ advisory│
└──────────────┘                   │  ├─A4 Policy──────────┤   │     └──────────┘  └────────────┘  └─────────┘
       │                           │  └─A5 Integrity───────┘   │
       └─ if extraction fails ─────┘   (run concurrently)      │
          → degrade / halt           fan-in: evidence bundle
```

| Stage | Components | Execution | Gate condition to proceed |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A — Extraction gate** | A1 (+T2) | Sequential | A1 returns a `CanonicalInvoice` with **at least the minimal key fields** (vendor, amount, currency, date) present at any confidence, OR returns `extraction_failed`. |
| **B — Verification fan-out** | A2, A3, A4, A5 | **Parallel** | All four resolve to `success` / `degraded` / `timeout` within branch budget. |
| **C — Scoring** | T1 | Sequential (deterministic) | Always runs once evidence bundle assembled (even partial). |
| **D — Narrative** | A6 | Sequential (LLM) | Always runs once score exists. |
| **E — Handoff** | AdvisoryHandoffBoundary | Sequential | Schema-valid `ReliabilityAssessment` with audit ID, score, explanation. |

