## 8. Timeout, Retry & Termination

### 8.1 Latency budget (against ≤30s median / ≤90s p95 SLA)

| Stage | Soft budget | Retry policy | On exhaustion |
|---|---|---|---|
| A — Extraction | 12s (OCR-heavy: up to 40s on p95 path) | 1 retry on transient OCR error | Halt or degrade (§8.3) |
| B — each branch (A2–A5) | 6s per branch (parallel) | 1 retry w/ backoff on transient/network error | Branch → `timeout`, `coverage:none` |
| B — stage deadline | 10s wall-clock (parallel) | — | Proceed with partial evidence |
| C — Scoring (T1) | <500ms | none (deterministic) | `failed` if engine error (should not happen) |
| D — Narrative (A6) | 5s | 1 regenerate on grounding failure | Fallback template |
| E — Handoff | 2s | 2 retries on delivery failure | Queue for async retry; job `completed`, delivery `pending` |

### 8.2 Termination conditions

| Terminal status | Condition | Output |
|---|---|---|
| `completed` | All stages succeeded; full coverage | Full `ReliabilityAssessment`, `human_decision_required: true` |
| `completed_with_degradation` | One or more branches `degraded`/`unverified`, but extraction gate passed and a defensible score produced | Assessment with explicit `unverified`/`partial` flags; band reflects reduced confidence |
| `failed` | Extraction gate not passable AND no usable canonical invoice; OR scoring engine fault | **No score emitted**; structured `failed` payload routed to **human triage queue** with reason; audit record complete |

> **Hard rule:** No terminal state ever sets approval/rejection. Even `failed` does **not** mean "reject" — it means "route to human." This preserves the 0-auto-approval invariant on every exit path.

### 8.3 Extraction-gate halt-vs-degrade decision

| Situation | Action |
|---|---|
| Minimal key fields present (any confidence) | **Degrade** → proceed to Stage B; flag low-confidence fields for HITL |
| Document unreadable / OCR total failure / corrupt file | **Halt** → `failed`, route to human triage (manual entry), with reason |
| Structured input fails schema parse | **Halt** → `failed` (cannot fabricate) |

